{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "06I1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-tangent-spaces}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:01ea751d0d5b0ab3b242c1248dc62e2e2d3c525aa100147cf9a91db5973f0487", "source_text": "Tangent spaces of predeformation categories", "source_text_hash": "sha256:57e77d745029d69544f40bce5819089cb8797b1e108828c4da90ee39411f661b", "unit_id": "tag:06I1:title"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06I1", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-tangent-space-over-R}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{example-tangent-space-functor}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:93a6ecad6182ac32a4df3f5853389d7de57b363ee229cefa0bbfcca21a2f0f0b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe will define tangent spaces of predeformation functors using the general\nDefinition <REF_0001>.\nWe have spelled this out in\nExample <REF_0002>.\nIt applies to predeformation categories by looking at the associated\nfunctor of isomorphism classes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1b746910d20c2df0ec246e827aafb97351e4cf075cb8ed12c530864f252fa593", "unit_id": "tag:06I1:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06I1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$T \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\overline{\\mathcal{F}}(k[\\epsilon])$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal\nF(k[\\epsilon])$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-tangent-space}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e6331eec828578ec629698fc65f405d768b882f9781e5bcf2eda85fb71d7d51", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:27246efc172a03c41e38988d8289162d26ba030f1e90b89c14f300937046844e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a predeformation category.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>tangent space <MATH_0002> of <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis the set <MATH_0004>\nof isomorphism classes of objects in the fiber category <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cae31d0fbf85f28023ba9a5db12de1b8548f98f678079bc33a7f9c3fa80994e6", "unit_id": "tag:06IG:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06I1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\overline{\\mathcal{F}}: \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\overline{\\mathcal{F}}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9d49f208c22c7d869f6b85915740cbcbf20cd3053b867d057f756d460e63f8e6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8f79e2579e3bfc85eeb4378ba956c0e5374c1fbe0dc4ef4add9e517f338e11ac", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThus <MATH_0001> is nothing but the tangent space of the associated\nfunctor <MATH_0002>.\nIt has a natural vector space structure when <MATH_0003> satisfies (S2),\nor, in fact, as long as <MATH_0004> does.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bb4ce7cd597af02204366731a722096fc4d89d19e04bfa51881d58662f133b14", "unit_id": "tag:06I1:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06I1", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\overline{\\mathcal{F}}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$T \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$k$", "MATH_0006": "$V$", "MATH_0007": "$\\overline{\\mathcal{F}}(k[V]) = T\\mathcal{F} \\otimes_k V$", "MATH_0008": "$V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-S1-S2-associated-functor}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-tangent-space-vector-space}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a621311be94d0b2a4f1720b89ab0f3a99a2b8f3142638a8c4b32219402df5a87", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3023870d4ccb76e089e5fb51c819537003abb35982be69d56e533599bd1dac87", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a predeformation category such that\n<MATH_0002> satisfies (S2)<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>For example\nif <MATH_0003> satisfies (S2), see\nLemma <REF_0001>.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>. Then <MATH_0004> has a\nnatural <MATH_0005>-vector space structure. For any finite dimensional\nvector space <MATH_0006> we have\n<MATH_0007>\nfunctorially in <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a0daaaf62bbb064b66541acd69ac0f48a133ed164ac17d63ea6964297335175d", "unit_id": "tag:06IH:statement"}
